Halo 64 ROM Builder - Custom Edition conversion tools (ce-tools)
=================================================================

This folder holds two kinds of programs:

  invader-build, invader-extract, invader-convert, invader-refactor,
  invader-bludgeon, invader-edit, invader-sound, invader-info,
  invader-dependency, invader-strip, invader-crc
      "invader-lite": Invader, a modding toolkit for Halo: Combat Evolved,
      built without its optional libraries (see below). Licensed under the
      GNU General Public License, version 3 only.

  ogg2wav
      An Ogg Vorbis to 16-bit PCM WAV decoder built on stb_vorbis. Public
      domain (or MIT, at your option).

They are command-line programs used by the Halo 64 ROM Builder. They contain
no game data. Content you extract or build with them keeps its own owner and
terms (see Invader's LICENSE.md: content made with Invader is not covered by
Invader's licence, and Invader gives no rights to existing game content).


